      "shortDescription": "Tronair designs and manufactures ground support equipment for aircraft operations and maintenance. Its official portfolio includes aircraft jacks and access stands, tugs and towbars, hydraulic and pressure-test equipment, ground-power units, service carts and engine-handling equipment.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Tronair is a United States manufacturer of aircraft ground support equipment. The company was founded in 1971 as Danair, adopted the Tronair name after a change of ownership in 1979 and is headquartered at Eugene F. Kranz Toledo Express Airport in Swanton, Ohio. Its equipment supports business and commercial aviation, aircraft manufacturers, maintenance organisations, defence contractors and military flight operations.",
        "The documented range covers axle and tripod jacks, maintenance stands and lifting equipment; aircraft tugs, towbars and towing accessories; hydraulic power units and fluid-service equipment; cabin-pressure test units; ground-power and air-conditioning equipment; nitrogen, oxygen, lavatory and potable-water service carts; landing-gear and brake-service tools; engine stands, slings and compressor-wash equipment. Tronair's current portfolio also includes the Eagle Tugs, Columbus Jack and Malabar International brands."
      ],
