      "statusModifier": "GROUP_BRAND",
      "shortDescription": "Tulsa Winch is a TWG brand for industrial winches, hoists and gear drives. Its official range includes worm-gear winches, planetary hoists, worm and planetary gear drives and associated load-handling configurations for infrastructure, energy, recovery and marine applications.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Tulsa Winch began in 1929 and today operates as one of the mechanical product brands within TWG, an operating company of Dover Corporation. The current official group site identifies Tulsa Winch, Inc. in Jenks, Oklahoma and presents Tulsa Winch alongside the DP Winch, Gear Products, Greer, Pullmaster, LANTEC and RUFNEK model lines.",
        "The Tulsa Winch product scope documented by TWG includes worm-gear winches, planetary hoists, worm-gear hoists, planetary and worm-gear drives and swing-drive configurations. These products are used in infrastructure, energy, vehicle recovery, natural-resource and marine applications, including large oilfield trucks, heavy-haul tractor packages, digger derricks, cranes and aerial work platforms. TWG's official resource library provides specifications, manuals and sales literature for the Tulsa Winch families."
