      "parentCompany": null,
      "shortDescription": "TURCK develops automation technology for factory, process and logistics applications. Its official portfolio spans industrial sensors, RFID identification, connectivity, decentralized I/O and fieldbus systems, interface and control technology, industrial networking, machine safety, vision, wireless and IIoT software.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "TURCK GmbH is a German family-owned automation company founded in 1965 and based in Mülheim an der Ruhr. The company develops and manufactures products and systems for factory, process and logistics automation, with production operations in Germany, Poland, the United States, Mexico and China.",
        "The documented portfolio extends from inductive, photoelectric, capacitive, ultrasonic, radar, position, pressure, temperature, flow and level sensors to RFID identification, cables and connectors, lighting and indicators, decentralized fieldbus and I/O systems, control-cabinet solutions, interface technology, industrial controls, power supplies, network components and machine-safety equipment. TURCK also supplies industrial wireless, cloud and vision solutions, the Snap Signal machine-data platform and the TURCK Automation Suite for commissioning, operation and industrial data use. Official application material covers food, pharmaceutical, chemical and automotive production, mobile machinery, intralogistics and packaging."
      ],
